  "diagram_notes": [
    {
      "content": "# **Any.Run URL Analysis**\n---- \n\nFill in the form with a suspicious URL and email and this story will create a Task on Any.run and analyse the URL. \n\nA simple result email will be sent to the provided email address. \n\n",
      "position": [
        930,
        -90
      ],
      "guid": "a768f904c896c9d91ada033fd3a4024a",
      "width": 290
    },
    {
      "content": "Continues only when ANY.RUN accepts the URL and returns HTTP `201 Created`.\n",
      "position": [
        105,
        240
      ],
      "guid": "f6e9ae0a9bc97a29a72d49d2331b9e07",
      "width": 290
    },
    {
      "content": "Continues when ANY.RUN returns HTTP `200 OK`.\n",
      "position": [
        840,
        510
      ],
      "guid": "d9155cc8cc62331cb2305c93361a3148",
      "width": 355
    },
    {
      "content": "Extracts the useful report details—URL, verdict, report link, hashes, and AI summary—into a simpler output for notification.\n",
      "position": [
        960,
        735
      ],
      "guid": "261170b9db85e58475233d88b99f5186",
      "width": 290
    },
    {
      "content": "Objective: Automate the safe triage of suspicious URLs by submitting them to ANY.RUN, monitoring the sandbox-analysis task, collecting the completed report and AI summary, and notifying the requester by email.\n",
      "position": [
        241,
        -174
      ],
      "guid": "a4ccc11ce84f59aa9079fd92b08724d7",
      "width": 960
    },
    {
      "content": "**Disclaimer**: This is a proof-of-concept playbook and is not production-ready. Before production use, implement access controls, URL and input validation, credential and secret management, error handling, monitoring, rate limiting, approval workflows, and organization-approved data-sharing, privacy, and retention policies. Only submit URLs that your organization is authorized to share with ANY.RUN.\n",
      "position": [
        240,
        -285
      ],
      "guid": "b707e65932863f353dca3af48c52f3a6",
      "width": 960
    }
  ],
